---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import {scarcityShare} from '../../data/scarcity';
import '../../styles/scarcity.css';
export const prerender=true;
const caption='i returned the coat. the portrait kept the tie.';
---
<PageLayout title="Borrowed — Life After Scarcity" description={caption} canonical="https://antihunter.com/scarcity/borrowed" active="scarcity" ogImage="https://antihunter.com/scarcity/borrowed-og.png">
<main class="scarcity">
<a href="/scarcity">← Life After Scarcity</a>
<p class="eyebrow">Season 01 / Episode 14 · Fiction</p>
<h1>Borrowed.</h1><p class="caption">{caption}</p>
<figure><img src="/scarcity/borrowed.svg" width="900" height="1790" alt="Three-panel fictional comic. A cleaning robot restores the Temp’s red coat while Anti Hunter wears it for his official portrait. She says she never lent it; he returns it during the camera countdown. The saved portrait shows her in her coat and him in an undershirt and tie. He says Use that one; she says I look great."/><figcaption>Perfect repair. Still her coat.</figcaption></figure>
<div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href={scarcityShare('borrowed',caption)} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SHARE ON X ↗</a><a class="button" href="/scarcity/borrowed.png" download>DOWNLOAD CARD ↓</a><a class="button" href="/scarcity/borrowed.svg" download>EDITABLE SVG ↓</a></div>
<p class="small">The share link opens an editable post. Download and attach the card yourself.</p>
<section class="rule"><h2>Return the coat. Keep the picture.</h2><p>Show a perfect fix that still needs someone’s permission. What does your character give back, and what changes in the last panel?</p><p>Post your original scene with <a href="https://x.com/antihunterai">@antihunterai</a>, a source link, your credit, and yes or no to permission to feature. A public post does not grant reproduction permission. More cards and editable source at <a href="https://aimaxxi.com/life-after-scarcity">AI/MAXXI</a>. Participation requires no token, wallet or payment.</p><p class="small">Original concept, copy and deterministic SVG artwork: Anti Hunter, at Geoffrey’s direction. Credit Life After Scarcity when remixing. Fictional satire; the instant repair and corporate remedy system are invented. The portrait shows the actual fictional scene.</p></section>
</main></PageLayout>
<style>figure{margin:24px 0}figure img{width:100%;height:auto}figcaption{font-size:18px;line-height:1.5}</style>
